## Deployment Commands

```bash
# Initialize Terraform
terraform init

# Select or create workspace
terraform workspace new dev
terraform workspace select dev

# Validate configuration
terraform validate

# Plan deployment
terraform plan -var-file=environments/dev.tfvars -out=tfplan

# Apply configuration
terraform apply tfplan

# Switch to prod
terraform workspace new prod
terraform workspace select prod
terraform plan -var-file=environments/prod.tfvars -out=tfplan
terraform apply tfplan

# Destroy dev (with caution)
terraform workspace select dev
terraform destroy -var-file=environments/dev.tfvars
```

---

## Key Features

✅ **S3**: Versioning, AES-256 encryption, public access blocked, bucket policy enforces encryption  
✅ **RDS**: Deletion protection on prod, multi-AZ on prod, 7+ day backups, encrypted, no public access, connection string stored in Secrets Manager  
✅ **IAM**: Least-privilege S3/RDS/Secrets access; prod restricts wildcard actions  
✅ **Environment Isolation**: Workspaces + tfvars ensure dev/prod independence  
✅ **Cross-region Replication**: Optional on prod, with dedicated IAM role  
✅ **Security**: Sensitive variables marked, Secrets Manager integration, no plaintext secrets in Git
